    fix(ready): emit pagination metadata on the proxied route too

    runReadyProxiedServer's JSON branch called the bare outputJSON(results)
    even though page.HasMore already carried enough information to detect
    truncation, so BD_JSON_ENVELOPE=1 consumers on the proxied path (the
    default for non-CGO/proxied builds) had no way to see the pagination
    signal that the direct route already exposes. Build a PaginationMeta
    with Returned/Truncated from page.HasMore && in.filter.Limit > 0 and
    route through outputJSONWithPagination instead; Total is left unset
    since this backend's domain page has no cheap total-count equivalent.

    Adds proxied-route coverage (pagination_envelope_truncated and
    pagination_envelope_not_truncated subtests) exercising the envelope
    under BD_JSON_ENVELOPE=1 for both truncated and non-truncated results.

    Closes the blocking item from the 2026-07-23 CHANGES_REQUESTED review
    on gastownhall/beads#4897.

